 the annexation of  crimea  and that's why uh as far uh as the  maritime security concerned ukraine is  most vulnerable from the  southern from the sea direction that's  why  these exercises along with the  building capacity of ukraine to defend  itself on the sea  is a really good move and i i would like  to say that uh  the rotational presence of the uh known  black sea nato countries  is really important and what we've seen  just a couple of  weeks ago with the hms defender who  uh touched a territorial waters of  ukraine uh around crimea that caused  a nervous reaction in kremlin it's a  right move to do  because freedom of negation is something  really important not just for ukraine  but the whole world and that's why uh  the whole world should support ukraine  showing that russia cannot set its rules  in the black sea area  all right alexander cara from the center  for defense strategies joining us from  kiev thank you so much  thank you
 

